  VIII. SYNTHESIS: THE ISING-TOURNAMENT DICTIONARY
  --------------------------------------------------

  TOURNAMENT          ISING MODEL
  ---------          -----------
  Tiling bit         Spin (+1/-1)
  Tournament T       Spin configuration
  H(T)               Energy E(config)
  Walsh coeff        Coupling constant
  Skip length        Interaction range
  Degree-1 Walsh     External field
  Degree-2 Walsh     Pairwise coupling
  Degree-3 Walsh     3-body interaction
  Transitive         Ground state (ordered)
  Random tournament  High-T state (disordered)
  Paley tournament   Excited state (frustrated)
  Flip chain         Glauber dynamics
  Spectral gap       Inverse relaxation time
  Walsh denom = 5    Golden-prime lattice
  H = 7 forbidden    Forbidden energy level

  The GOLDEN PRIME 5 controls the lattice spacing
  of the eigenvalue spectrum (all nontrivial eigenvalues
  are multiples of 1/5). This is the crystallographic
  structure of tournament space viewed as a lattice gas.

  The phase transition (peak specific heat) occurs near
  beta = 0 (uniform distribution). This means:
  RANDOM TOURNAMENTS ARE AT THE CRITICAL POINT.
  The flip chain at uniform temperature is maximally
  susceptible — small perturbations create large H changes.
  This is WHY random tournaments are computationally HARD
  (Regime 42, no shortcut).

